  "abstract": {
    "value": "Eficient deoxygenative silylation of $\\mathrm { C } ( \\mathsf { s p } ^ { 3 } ) \\mathrm { - O }$ bonds with hydrosilanes by supported Au catalysts is described. Gold nanoparticles supported on $\\mathrm { T i O } _ { 2 }$ enabled various hydrosilanes to be used as sources of silyl groups in C−Si cross-coupling reactions. A variety of alkyl acetates and propargyl carbonates participated in the Au-catalyzed reactions to furnish the corresponding alkyl and allenylsilanes in high yields. In addition,",
